#
# Conformance case: teleology/observation-conditioned-policy.
#
# An action schema (senseSchema) declares a logic:observation (sensorReading) that
# logic:reveals obstacleDetected. A plan with two observation-conditioned branches —
# avoidBranch guarded on obstacleDetected, proceedBranch guarded on pathClear — is a
# POLICY: its next action is chosen from what the observation reveals, not fixed in
# advance. The engine surfaces the observation's reveal, then selects the matching
# branch (avoidBranch) and its logic:nextActionSchema (rerouteSchema); the non-matching
# proceedBranch is NOT selected.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom the
# projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/observation-conditioned-policy/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
